This is a known breaking change. Android deprecated `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE` (API 30+), and .NET MAUI's edge-to-edge support in .NET 9+ means the old `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` no longer reliably pushes content up.

**The modern fix** — listen to keyboard (IME) insets on Android and adjust your layout padding:

**1. In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:**

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Platform;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Enable edge-to-edge insets handling
        WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);
        Window!.SetSoftInputMode(SoftInput.AdjustResize);
    }
}
```

**2. Add a behavior or handler that reacts to IME insets.** In `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureMauiHandlers(handlers =>
{
#if ANDROID
    Microsoft.Maui.Handlers.PageHandler.Mapper.AppendToMapping(
        "KeyboardPadding", (handler, view) =>
    {
        var platformView = handler.PlatformView;
        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(platformView, new KeyboardInsetsListener());
    });
#endif
});
```

**3. Create `Platforms/Android/KeyboardInsetsListener.cs`:**

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.Graphics;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

public class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View view, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

        // Use the larger of IME or nav bar bottom inset
        int bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);

        view.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

        return insets;
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` gives you the keyboard height
- You apply that as bottom padding so your input bar shifts up
- This replaces the old `Resize` mode and works on all Android versions
- **iOS** handles this automatically — no changes needed there

If you want a **quick-and-dirty alternative**, `SoftInput.AdjustPan` still works — it scrolls the focused `Entry` into view — but it doesn't shrink your layout, so it's less ideal for chat UIs.
